[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:8. A Famous Monastery]
[00:00.640] Passage 8. | 第八篇课文。
[00:01.830] A famous monastery. | 著名的修道院。
[00:04.435] The Great St Bernard Pass connects Switzerland to Italy. | 大圣伯纳德山口连接着瑞士和意大利。
[00:09.165] At 8,114 feet, | 海拔8114英尺，
[00:12.035] it is the highest mountain pass in Europe. | 它是欧洲最高的山口。
[00:14.915] The famous monastery of St Bernard, | 著名的圣伯纳德修道院，
[00:17.580] which was founded in the 11th century, lies about a mile away. | 建于11世纪，位于大约一英里之外。
[00:21.325] For hundreds of years St Bernard dogs have saved the lives of travellers crossing the dangerous pass. | 几百年来，圣伯纳德犬拯救了穿越这个危险山口的旅行者的生命。
[00:27.540] These friendly dogs, which were first brought from Asia, | 这些友善的狗，最初是从亚洲带过来的，
[00:31.170] were used as watchdogs even in Roman times. | 甚至在罗马时代就被用作看门狗。
[00:34.530] Now that a tunnel has been built through the mountains, | 如今，一条隧道已经穿山而过，
[00:37.295] the pass is less dangerous. | 这个山口就不那么危险了。
[00:39.225] But each year the dogs are still sent out into the snow, | 但每年，只要有旅行者遇到困难，
[00:42.755] whenever a traveller is in difficulty. | 狗仍然会被派到雪地里。
[00:45.360] Despite the new tunnel, | 尽管有了新隧道，
[00:47.405] there are still a few people who rashly attempt to cross the pass on foot. | 仍然有一些人贸然徒步穿越山口。
[00:52.360] During the summer months, the monastery is very busy. | 在夏季，修道院非常繁忙。
[00:56.135] For it is visited by thousands of people who cross the pass in cars. | 因为有成千上万驾车穿越山口的人会来参观。
[01:00.475] As there are so many people about, | 由于人来人往，
[01:02.625] the dogs have to be kept in a special enclosure. | 那些狗必须被关在一个特殊的围栏里。
[01:05.835] In winter, however, | 然而，在冬天，
[01:07.725] life at the monastery is quite different. | 修道院的生活则大不相同。
[01:10.585] The temperature drops to minus 30 degrees, | 气温降至零下30摄氏度，
[01:13.850] and very few people attempt to cross the pass. | 很少有人会尝试穿越山口。
[01:17.200] The monks prefer winter to summer, | 僧侣们更喜欢冬天而不是夏天，
[01:19.820] for they have more privacy. | 因为他们有更多的隐私。
[01:21.685] The dogs have greater freedom too. | 狗也有更大的自由。
[01:24.440] For they are allowed to wander outside their enclosure. | 因为它们被允许在围栏外自由漫步。
[01:27.840] The only regular visitors to the monastery in winter | 冬天里修道院唯一的常客
[01:31.155] are parties of skiers who go there at Christmas and Easter. | 是在圣诞节和复活节去那里的滑雪者。
[01:35.020] These young people, who love the peace of the mountains, | 这些热爱山区宁静的年轻人，
[01:38.745] always receive a warm welcome | 总能得到热情的欢迎
[01:41.150] at St Bernard's monastery. | 在圣伯纳德修道院。